    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d274">

                <pb facs="0274" n="262" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg262"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860C.20/94: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-11-14T16:00:00+03:00">November 14, 1941—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 15—12:36 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1924. Department’s 1197, November 7, 7 p.m. I received from Vyshinski<anchor
                        n="24" xml:id="d274-f1"/> this noon the following personal message from
                    Stalin to Harriman in reply to the latter’s message of November 7: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I received your telegram on November 12.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d274-f2"
                            /> I have not yet had an opportunity to acquaint myself with the details
                            of the matter of the Poles in the U. S. S. R. After two or three days
                            and having studied the matter, I will inform you of the position of the
                            Soviet Government. I do not doubt that the desires of the Poles and the
                            interests of the friendly relations between the U. S. S. R. [and] Poland
                            will be definitely taken into consideration by the Soviet
                            Government.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d274-f1" n="24" xml:id="d274-f1-content">
                <p>Audrey Yanuaryevich Vyshinsky, Assistant People’s Commissar for Foreign Affairs
                    of the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d274-f2" n="25" xml:id="d274-f2-content">
                <p>Ambassador Steinhardt had left with Vyshinsky on November 10, 1941, a paraphrase
                    of Harriman’s message for delivery to Stalin.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
